{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"readAndUpdate","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["iOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"All tile requests are converted to tile pack requests, i.e.","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the tile pack that includes the request tile will be loaded, and the tile extracted","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"from it. In this mode, no individual tile requests will be made.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This mode can be useful if the map trajectory is predefined and the user cannot pan","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"freely (e.g. navigation use cases), so that there is a good chance tile packs are already loaded"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in the vicinity of the user.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If users can pan freely, this mode is not recommended. Otherwise, panning"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"will download tile packs instead of using individual tiles. Note that this means that we could first"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"download an individual tile, and then a tile pack that also includes this tile. The individual tile in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"the disk cache won’t be used as long as the up-to-date tile pack exists in the cache.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","externalID":"c:@E@MBMTileStoreUsageMode@MBMTileStoreUsageModeReadAndUpdate","roleHeading":"Case","modules":[{"name":"MapboxMaps"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"readAndUpdate","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"TileStoreUsageMode.readAndUpdate","symbolK